    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier option, boasting an elite score of 81.88. His high-leadoff placement, combined with a plus matchup against Burke and a park factor boost, makes him the engine of our attack. **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** also offer excellent returns in the same contest against Baz; both benefit significantly from a favorable park environment and top-of-the-order protections. While **Heliot Ramos** sits in the middle of the pack, his matchup against Rodriguez is bolstered by a favorable park and potential stolen base opportunities against a slow-delivering pitcher, making him a sneaky high-floor play despite the lack of a platoon advantage.\n\nConversely, our outfield deployment requires careful monitoring, particularly with **Josh Lowe**, whose status remains contingent on a pending lineup announcement. We are also wary of **Jackson Merrill**; despite the wind blowing out, his unfavorable platoon split against Imanaga suppresses his efficiency score to 52.05, placing him near the bottom of our starters. Our most difficult bench decision was **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 46.15 score. While his placement in the #2 spot usually provides a boost, the combination of a difficult matchup against the lefty Messick and our internal preference for high-volume scoring players kept him out of the starting nine. We will look for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nolan Schanuel**, and **Curtis Mead** to provide late-inning impact should our starters struggle to capitalize against their respective left-handed matchups.",
